posts.body:
if it flickers, use this hacky way boot
Code:
show picture 1 opacity 0 // slash1
wait 1
show picture 1 opacity 0 slash2
wait 1
etc
...
erase pictre 1
if it has a bunch, you can use galv or entire folder what I use on boot
from base plugin
JavaScript:
SDJB_Base.preloadFolders = function() {
        // A list of preloaded images used by my plugins and others
        if (Imported["SDJB_TitleRewardIcons"]) {
            ImageManager.loadTRI = function(filename, hue) {
                return this.loadBitmap("img/shadowdragon/tri/", filename, hue, true);
            }
        }
        // load folder here or list
    }

    SDJB_Base._SB_start = Scene_Boot.prototype.start;
        Scene_Boot.prototype.start = function() {
            SDJB_Base.preloadFolders();
            SDJB_Base._SB_start.apply(this, arguments);

        };
so from this, it load all images from boot, so you can set img/pictures
and it load all pictures in the pictures folder, as its simple and effective.
it depends how much images needed to be loaded.
if its only 20, use the evented way, or a smaller plugin to load a common event
on boot (which I have on it too) and turn it off, so its always loaded when the
game starts.
so you don't have to worry to much anyway
so try some pictures of the slash on evented way and see if that fixed,
than use galv plugin (as it can load the folder) and/or images required.
from there, if it works, your good to go

